WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.533
Tier one.

2
00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:05.539
These are the skills every twenty five lakh posting asks for.

3
00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:08.333
Miss any of them and the conversation is over.

4
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:11.587
Count them: nine skills in total.

5
00:00:11.587 --> 00:00:16.067
All non-negotiable, no matter how strong the rest of your profile looks.

6
00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.467
This is a hard filter, not a wish list.

7
00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:23.567
Miss any one of these, and a strong profile elsewhere will not save you.

8
00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:27.567
Here is how often each skill shows up in postings.

9
00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:31.083
Production Python is in every single one.

10
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:36.967
RAG and LLM APIs appear in ninety five percent, vector databases in ninety.

11
00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:43.351
Prompting and MLOps sit at eighty five, agents at eighty, evaluation at seventy five.

12
00:00:43.351 --> 00:00:46.500
Cost optimization comes in at sixty percent.

13
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.665
The keywords are the same, but the depth is different.

14
00:00:50.665 --> 00:00:51.433
Let's compare.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:55.667
Python means tested, typed, documented code, not notebooks.

16
00:00:55.967 --> 00:01:02.900
LLM API integration means several providers with fallback and routing, not one hardcoded client.

17
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.833
And prompt engineering means templates, caching and few-shot calibration, versioned like code.

18
00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:11.490
RAG is the next big one.

19
00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.100
They want the pipeline designed end to end.

20
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.167
First, chunking your documents.

21
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:17.833
Then embedding each chunk.

22
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:23.900
Then retrieval, from a vector database like pgvector, Qdrant, Pinecone or Weaviate.

23
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.567
And finally reranking, so the best passages come first.

24
00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:29.595
Let's recap.

25
00:01:29.595 --> 00:01:31.733
Nine skills are non-negotiable.

26
00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:37.000
Python, RAG, LLM APIs and vector databases lead the list.

27
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.300
Employers want production depth, not notebook demos.

28
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.083
And evaluation and cost close it out.

29
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:45.700
Next up: Tier two, the pay multipliers.
